tnoodle-native 0.1.0

This is an unofficial derivative of TNoodle, not an official WCA scramble
program and not endorsed by the World Cube Association.

The scrambling and drawing engine derives from:
  https://github.com/thewca/tnoodle-lib
  v0.20.0, commit b7f9bfeca5d43856e551e975ba305c36a3b86fcb
  GNU GPL version 3. See LICENSE and tools/native/upstream.

The original authors include Jeremy Fleischman, Shuang Chen and the other
TNoodle contributors identified in the preserved source headers and history.
min2phase and threephase: Copyright Shuang Chen, GPL version 3 or later.
The combined port is distributed under GPL-3.0-only. This does not remove
the additional permissions individual upstream files grant.

Modifications in this port:
  - Ahead-of-time translation to standalone CommonJS JavaScript with TeaVM.
  - Explicit Java-compatible integer rejection sampling backed by node:crypto.
  - Removal of JVM SecureRandom providers and seeded production APIs.
  - Fixed default 3x3 distance configuration (no JVM environment override).
  - Removal of private-move/debug logs; explicit errors on 3x3 solver failure.
  - XML escaping in the svglite serializer.
  - Native bridge, development diagnostics, TypeScript API and worker scheduling.
  - New PDF/ZIP document layout implemented independently using Node libraries.

tools/native/prepare.mjs records all source adaptations. The unmodified engine
sources, development bridge, build instructions and source checksums are
included as corresponding source. Java/Maven are development tools only;
no Java runtime, JVM, bytecode interpreter or WebAssembly is shipped/required
by the runtime entry point. TeaVM emits direct JavaScript and only reachable
class-library helpers, not the entire JRE.

Generated code includes TeaVM runtime/class-library helpers, Apache-2.0:
  Copyright Alexey Andreev and contributors.
  See licenses/TeaVM-LICENSE and licenses/TeaVM-NOTICE.

Runtime dependencies:
  pdfkit 0.17.2: MIT, Copyright Devon Govett and contributors.
  svg-to-pdfkit 0.1.8: MIT, Copyright SVG-to-PDFKit contributors.
  fflate 0.8.2: MIT, Copyright Arjun Barrett.
Their license texts are included in licenses and in their npm packages.
Their transitive dependencies retain their individual license notices.

The AGPL-3.0 TNoodle server was consulted for event/export concepts only;
no Kotlin server, iText, server PDF templates, logos or UI code is copied.
The current event catalog is fixed to the 17 events in WCA Regulation 9b,
checked on 2026-10-16. FTO is not included in the public API.

